 ## Background
-Early researchers using LCD SLMs or magneto-optic SLMs created small planar images [S1, S14, S3, S5]. The challenge in holographic displays arises from the many millions of samples in a fringe, which successful approaches address by exploiting parallelism and/or the time-response of the human visual system (typically 20 ms) [S1]. Reflective LCDs created directly on semiconductor chips using VLSI technology have also been explored [S15].
